      "ownershipVehicle": "Axium Infrastructure Canada II Limited Partnership / Axium TransCo LP",
      "description": "PUC Transmission LP is an Ontario regulated transmitter developing, financing, constructing and operating Tagona West Transformer Station and an approximately 10 route-kilometre, dual-circuit 230 kV transmission line in Sault Ste. Marie. The approximately C$230 million project will provide about 300 MW of new load to Algoma Steel's electric-arc-furnace operations while strengthening regional reliability and capacity. The line comprises approximately 20 circuit-kilometres across two 400 MVA circuits. Axium Infrastructure holds 80% through the disclosed Axium Infrastructure Canada II Limited Partnership / Axium TransCo chain, while PUC Inc. retains 20%. The OEB granted leave to construct on August 27, 2024 and issued electricity transmission licence ET-2021-0088 on April 10, 2025. Current company materials target construction completion in Q1 2028 and energization in January 2028. No later ownership transfer or signed pending exit was identified through August 18, 2026.",
